      "Critics argue that the dominance of English threatens other languages and cultures. As young people increasingly use English for work and entertainment, some smaller languages are spoken less and may eventually disappear, taking with them traditional knowledge, stories and ways of thinking. There is also a risk that native English speakers gain an unfair advantage in international settings. These concerns are valid, but they do not mean that the spread of English is negative in itself. Many people around the world are bilingual, using English for international purposes while continuing to speak their own language at home, and governments can protect local languages through education and cultural programmes.",
